title: Menus
manual:

The menu bar holds the commands that do not belong to one window. Default key bindings
are given in parentheses (changeable in Edit > Preferences).

# File

- "New..." (Ctrl+Shift+N), "New from Library..." and "New Molecule" (Ctrl+N) create a
  structure from scratch, from the critic2 library, or an empty molecule.
- "Open..." (Ctrl+O) reads structures from files; "Duplicate", "Restore" (Ctrl+R)
  and "Close" (Ctrl+W) act on the current system.
- "Export to PNG" (Ctrl+E) writes an image of the view next to the source file; "Export
  to Image..." (Ctrl+Shift+E) asks for the file and settings; "Export to 3D Model..."
  writes a 3D model file.
- "Save" (Ctrl+S) writes the current system back to its input file, "Save As..."
  (Ctrl+Shift+S) in a chosen format, "Save Multiple..." several systems at once and
  "Save Scene..." the system as shown.
- "Load Field..." and "Load Field from File..." load a scalar field.
- "Demonstrations": "Water Cluster" and "Metal Melting".
- "Quit" (Ctrl+Q).

# Edit

- "Undo" (Ctrl+Z) and "Redo" (Ctrl+Y, Ctrl+Shift+Z) revert or repeat the last change to
  the geometry or the objects.
- "Cut" (Ctrl+X), "Copy" (Ctrl+C) and "Paste" (Ctrl+V) move the selected atoms through
  the clipboard. "Paste as..." makes a "New Molecule" or "New Crystal" from it. "Remove
  Selection" (Delete) deletes them.
- "Select All" (Ctrl+A), "Select None" (Escape) and "Invert Selection" change the
  selection; "System from Selection" and "Molecule from Selection" make a new system
  from it.
- "Preferences..." (Ctrl+,) opens the settings and key bindings window; "Reset
  Preferences" restores the defaults.

# Windows

- "Tree" (F2), "Main View", "Input Console" (F3) and "Output Console" (F4) show or hide
  the permanent windows; "Display Settings" selects the part of the system drawn in the
  main view; "New View Window" opens an additional view.
- "Save Layout" stores the window positions for the next start; "Reset Layout" docks
  the permanent windows in their default places.

# Tools

The tool windows, described in the other help topics.

- "Recalculate Bonds" (F5), "View/Edit Geometry..." (G), "Builder..." (Ctrl+B) and
  "Extract Molecule(s)..." act on the structure.
- "Dynamics": "Vibrations...", "Dynamics...", "Rattle Structure...".
- "Structure Analysis": "Crystal Voids...", "K-Point Grid...", "K-Path Selection...".
- "Field Plots": "Point Properties...", "Line Profile...", "Plane Map...",
  "Isosurface...", "Calculate Grid...", "NCI Plot...", "Molecular Orbitals...".
- "QTAIM": "Critical Points...", "Trace Gradient Paths...".

# Help

- "Help Topics..." opens this window, "Critic2 Manual..." (F1) the online manual and
  "About..." the version and references.
